<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Live Map — SiteGuard Main Admin</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
<div class="admin-shell">
  <%- include('../partials/main-admin-sidebar', { active: 'live-map' }) %>

  <div class="admin-main">
    <div class="admin-topline">
      <h1>Live Map</h1>
      <form class="logout-form" method="POST" action="/main-admin/logout">
        <button type="submit">Log out (<%= mainAdminName %>)</button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <% if (TRACCAR_WEB_URL) { %>
      <div class="admin-card" style="padding:0; overflow:hidden;">
        <iframe src="<%= TRACCAR_WEB_URL %>" style="width:100%; height:75vh; border:none; display:block;" title="Traccar Live Map"></iframe>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:12px; color:var(--steel); margin-top:10px;">
        Loaded from your Traccar server's own web interface (<%= TRACCAR_WEB_URL %>). Log in there with your Traccar
        account to see live driver positions, history, and geofences.
      </p>
    <% } else { %>
      <div class="admin-card">
        <h3>Live tracking isn't set up yet</h3>
        <p>
          SiteGuard can show live driver locations here, powered by
          <a href="https://www.traccar.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Traccar</a> — a free, self-hosted GPS
          tracking server. The Driver App is already wired to report location once this is configured; nothing
          else needs to change in SiteGuard.
        </p>
        <h4 style="margin-top:20px;">To enable it</h4>
        <ol style="font-size:14px; line-height:1.8;">
          <li>Host a Traccar server (e.g. via their <a href="https://www.traccar.org/download/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Docker image</a> on any VPS you control).</li>
          <li>In SiteGuard's <code>.env</code>, set <code>TRACCAR_SERVER_URL</code> to the Traccar OsmAnd reporting port (default <code>:5055</code>) and <code>TRACCAR_WEB_URL</code> to its web UI (default <code>:8082</code>), then restart the app.</li>
          <li>In the Traccar web UI, register a device for each driver below using the exact Device ID shown, or enable "Allow auto registration" in Traccar's server settings so they register themselves the first time a driver's app reports a position.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="admin-card">
        <h3>Driver Device IDs</h3>
        <div class="data-table-wrap">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Driver</th><th>Traccar Device ID</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <% if (drivers.length === 0) { %>
                <tr><td colspan="2" style="text-align:center; color:#8a8f90;">No drivers yet.</td></tr>
              <% } %>
              <% drivers.forEach(d => { %>
                <tr><td><%= d.name %></td><td><code>driver-<%= d.id %></code></td></tr>
              <% }) %>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
